From: Stackfort Authors <noreply@stackfort.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Emit sanitized rule events through the nginx error log

libcoraza exposes a matched-rule callback, but coraza-nginx 0.20.0 does not
connect it to nginx. Register the callback for every worker-local WAF and bind
the currently evaluated request around each Coraza rule phase. The callback
emits only the rule ID, severity, connector-generated request correlation,
method, and normalized queryless URI. It deliberately never requests or logs
Coraza's match data, message, request headers, query string, or body.
